+## Appendix A — Reference-screen content checklist
+
+The supplied doctor-profile screenshot is a visual/content reference. The production profile should render real saved values for:
+
+- Connected status.
+- Doctor name and credentials.
+- Specialty/specialization.
+- Gender and displayed age where configured and appropriate.
+- Hospital/working location and city/area.
+- Years of experience.
+- “Part of your care team” relationship.
+- “Contact care team” action and approved phone/contact route.
+
+The reference's example person, values, and hospital must not be copied into production patient records. Empty profile values should use an explicit “Not provided” state or an appropriate fallback, not blank space.
+
+## Appendix B — Domain objects for engineering estimation
+
+Initial entities should include `organizations`, `locations`, `users`, `staff_profiles`, `role_templates`, `permissions`, `care_teams`, `team_memberships`, `patients`, `patient_assignments`, `consents`, `qr_invitations`, `encounters`, `reports`, `report_files`, `medications`, `care_plans`, `care_plan_milestones`, `appointments`, `follow_up_tasks`, `contact_attempts`, `notifications`, and `audit_events`.
+
+Use stable IDs and organization scoping on every tenant-owned record. Define foreign keys, indexes, retention behavior, row-level access rules, and allowed state transitions before implementation. Store files separately from structured report metadata and serve them through authorized, expiring access.
